{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "label": "Log platform integrations", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlp_first", "label": "OTLP first", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One endpoint format reaches the OpenTelemetry Collector, Loki 3+, Parseable, SigNoz, Datadog, Axiom, Honeycomb and New Relic, so a native sink only earns its place where OTLP does not reach or loses something."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlphttpsink", "label": "OtlpHttpSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emits an ExportLogsServiceRequest in proto3 JSON with no protobuf library and no OpenTelemetry SDK; service.name defaults to the actor system name because the thing a backend groups by should say what the service is called, not what the library is called."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_no_otel_logs_sdk", "label": "Why not the OpenTelemetry logs SDK", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The reason is asymmetric with tracing: the protocol is stable and its JSON encoding is specified, while the JavaScript logs SDK is still an experimental 0.x whose releases may break. A fixed wire format is the safer thing to build on - and otelLogger exists for records that should flow through the SDK pipeline instead."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlp_retry_rule", "label": "OTLP retry rule", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Follows the specification: 429, 502, 503 and 504 are retried honouring Retry-After, everything else is not. A 400 or a 401 describes the request, and sending it again unchanged cannot produce a different answer, so it is dropped and reported once rather than retried five times against a service that will never accept it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelfsink", "label": "GelfSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Graylog is the one platform the OTLP sink cannot reach, because its OpenTelemetry input accepts OTLP over gRPC only; GELF also lands structured fields as first-class searchable keys where the OTLP route prefixes them."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelf_field_name_safety", "label": "GELF field-name safety", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The MDC can carry values that arrived from a remote cluster peer, so additional-field names are sanitised to what the spec allows, the forbidden _id is dropped, and a field that would land on one of GELF own top-level keys is dropped rather than allowed to overwrite it. A peer cannot rewrite the message it is reporting."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelf_transports", "label": "GELF transport choice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "udp is the default and what a stock Graylog input listens on, compressed and chunked with max-chunk-bytes at 1420 so the packet stays inside a 1500-byte MTU with room for a tunnel header; tcp when losing a datagram is unacceptable or TLS is needed; http behind a proxy. A document too large for 128 chunks is dropped rather than retried, because retrying cannot make it smaller."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_parseablesink", "label": "ParseableSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records are sent flat because Parseable flattens nested objects at ingest anyway, which keeps every field individually queryable and skips a round of server-side rewriting. A batch over the 10 MiB request cap is split rather than truncated, because exceeding it is not a retryable failure - the server rejects the whole request, so an oversized batch would be lost in full."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_lokisink", "label": "LokiSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One push in plain JSON, which Loki accepts as an alternative to snappy-compressed protobuf so no compression or protobuf library is involved. The timestamp is a nanosecond string because Loki answers a JSON number with a 400 and the value is past what a double holds exactly."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_loki_static_labels", "label": "Loki labels stay static", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Labels are Loki index and every distinct combination is a separate stream, so a per-record value - an actor path, a request id - multiplies streams without bound and is the standard way to make a Loki cluster unusable. The options type therefore refuses a label derived from the record; variable data goes into structured metadata, which Loki stores per entry instead of indexing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_seqsink", "label": "SeqSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Newline-delimited CLEF, which is the NDJSON the framework already emits with four keys renamed. Levels use the Serilog vocabulary so info becomes Information - the one value that is easy to get wrong and that Seq rejects. An at-prefixed field name has its sigil doubled per CLEF own escaping rule, so a reserved key arriving over the cluster wire cannot forge the record timestamp."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_splunksink", "label": "SplunkSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Events are concatenated back to back rather than wrapped in a JSON array, because concatenation is the batch format every version understands and the difference is one join. The indexed fields key must be flat and only works on the event endpoint, which is why this sink never uses raw."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentrysink", "label": "Sentry sink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "You pass your own SDK: the framework never imports it, declares no dependency and has no version to keep in step, and more importantly it uses the client your application already configured so releases, environments and breadcrumbs line up instead of competing. That is also why there is no HOCON block - the sink needs a live SDK object, which a config file cannot hold."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentry_warning_is_not_an_issue", "label": "A warning is not an issue", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turning a warning into a tracked, assignable, alert-firing event is how a Sentry project becomes noise nobody reads, so warnings go to logs and only errors become issues. The default level is warn - stricter than every other sink - because Sentry is priced per event: pointing a debug firehose at it is a billing incident, and the signal an on-call engineer depends on drowns either way."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentry_no_hand_rolled_envelope", "label": "Why not hand-roll the Sentry wire protocol", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The envelope format is documented and could be built without a dependency, but what makes Sentry useful is grouping, stack-trace processing, release detection and breadcrumbs - all of which live in the SDK, and all of which a hand-rolled transport would either duplicate badly or lose."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslogsink", "label": "SyslogSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The integration that needs no vendor: rsyslog, syslog-ng, the journald forwarder, Papertrail and a long tail of network appliances all speak RFC 5424. Facility defaults to 16 (local0), the range reserved for applications, because below it belongs to the system where an application records would be misfiled."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslog_framing", "label": "Syslog framing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "octet-counting is the default and the only framing that survives a message containing a newline, which a stack trace always does; the length is counted in bytes so a multi-byte character cannot make the receiver cut the frame short. The lf framing collapses newlines to spaces because it cannot represent them."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslog_structured_data_dash", "label": "The structured-data element is a dash", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A well-formed SD-ID requires an IANA private enterprise number, and inventing one would file records under somebody else identifier. The record fields are appended to MSG in the same form the console uses, so nothing is lost - it is simply not machine-parsed by the receiver. Revisitable if the project ever registers a number."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_code_only_credentials", "label": "Credentials and TLS material are code-only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "headers, TLS material and SDK objects have no HOCON leaf: an API key in a config file ends up in version control, and the TLS fields carry the certificate and key themselves rather than paths to them."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlp_first", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlphttpsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_no_otel_logs_sdk", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlp_retry_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelfsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelf_field_name_safety", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelf_transports", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_parseablesink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_lokisink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_loki_static_labels", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_seqsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_splunksink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentrysink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentry_warning_is_not_an_issue", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentry_no_hand_rolled_envelope", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslogsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslog_framing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslog_structured_data_dash", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_code_only_credentials", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlp_first", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_no_otel_logs_sdk", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlphttpsink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlp_retry_rule", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_otlphttpsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelf_field_name_safety", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelfsink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelf_transports", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_gelfsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_loki_static_labels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_lokisink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentry_warning_is_not_an_issue", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentrysink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentry_no_hand_rolled_envelope", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_sentrysink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslog_framing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslogsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslog_structured_data_dash", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_syslogsink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_code_only_credentials", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_integrations_log_platform_integrations", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/integrations.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"